  // The rider, in parts of boxes that only touch (never overlap), so they sort right without a depth buffer, each
  // turned on its own so the body moves: the board or skis with the boots, a shin and a thigh on each leg (the knees
  // bend), the body and head (from the hips: jacket with a stripe, backpack, neck gaiter, mirrored goggles, helmet),
  // an upper arm and a forearm with its glove on each side (and a pole on skis), and the gaiter's end streaming out
  // behind. Every part is built facing +x (the chest), shoulders along z. On a board, the board runs along z and the
  // rider goes +z, sideways; on skis, they run along x and the whole rider is turned to go chest first.
  // Outfits: jacket (c, d darker), accent (b: the board, the stripe and the scarf), pants (p) and helmet (h).
  let JACKETS = [
    {c: #e8412f, d: #a82a1e, b: #ffd34a, p: #23262e, h: #f4f4f4},
    {c: #2b6cb0, d: #1b4a80, b: #ff7a2f, p: #e9e4d8, h: #1b1b1e},
